{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines","id":36040,"title":"B&S 'Lashing Out' against Disciplines.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T20:03:58-08:00","id":36040,"title":"B&S 'Lashing Out' against Disciplines.","content":"Majesty1 (Awe) and Nightmare1 (Dread Presence) both have no activation roll, no cost, and state that the only way for Kindred to resist is by 'Lashing Out' and reference the Lashing Out page. However, that section does not at all comment upon using 'Lashing Out' in this fashion.<br /> <br /> So how precisely does this work? Do other Vampires have to spend a Willpower point (which you normally do to 'Lash Out') just to try and resist these Disciplines? And what are the mechanics for the Lashing Out in this situation. Is it a contested Lashing Out as normal, or do I just roll PowerAttribute+BP and if I get a success I resist the power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1796-tempest","name":"Tempest","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T03:42:10-08:00","id":36283,"title":"","content":"You treat it like a normal predatory aura Lash Out. The vampire who doesn't want to be affected by the power picks an aspect of the Beast and rolls it, then the vampire using the power acts as the defender and chooses fight or flight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T11:46:50-08:00","id":37426,"title":"","content":"With this in mind, is it possible to selectively decide that you don't want to include certain individuals in the effects of Majesty/Nightmare?<br /> Say you want to awe a room but there is this monstrous and potent Gangrel in the corner that <b>will</b> lash out and be cranky if you Awe them.<br /> Would a vampire be able to Awe the room and rule out that person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T12:15:22-08:00","id":37440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyoseph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37426#post37426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this in mind, is it possible to selectively decide that you don't want to include certain individuals in the effects of Majesty/Nightmare?<br /> Say you want to awe a room but there is this monstrous and potent Gangrel in the corner that <b>will</b> lash out and be cranky if you Awe them.<br /> Would a vampire be able to Awe the room and rule out that person?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T13:28:47-08:00","id":37484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37440#post37440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't see why not.</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally, I think its realistic hazard of using mind-affecting powers that target large groups of people. You shouldn't be able to just turn on your love beams in a crowded room and expect no one to push back. And I don't think its reasonable to say &quot;well I'm only trying to impress the people who won't mind it&quot;. But that's just my personal taste, I like discipline use to always be a calculated risk. If that's not your bag, by all means allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T19:37:32-08:00","id":37618,"title":"","content":"The main cause for my concern there is the &quot;building block&quot; nature of the disciplines in question. Particularly Majesty. In order to use Confidant, you must have an Awed target. In order to use Green Eyes, must have a Confidant'ed or Loyalty'ed target. In order to use Loyalty, must have a Confidant'ed target. If Lashing Out does more than just turn the discipline off, then having that cranky bastard in the corner pretty much kills the Daeva's signature social Discipline unless they want to resort to the sledgehammer that is Idol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T20:47:16-08:00","id":37660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyoseph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37618#post37618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main cause for my concern there is the &quot;building block&quot; nature of the disciplines in question. Particularly Majesty. In order to use Confidant, you must have an Awed target. In order to use Green Eyes, must have a Confidant'ed or Loyalty'ed target. In order to use Loyalty, must have a Confidant'ed target. If Lashing Out does more than just turn the discipline off, then having that cranky bastard in the corner pretty much kills the Daeva's signature social Discipline unless they want to resort to the sledgehammer that is Idol.</div> </div> </div> </div> Only for that one guy who Lashed Out though, everyone else is still affected, or so I thought. And anyway, it's not like that guy can't Lash Out at you if you don't use Majesty, so if Bestial, Competitive, or Wanton was going to ruin your day, it'd do so regardless of your disciplines. And like I said, I like discipline use to always be a risk in my games, so the fact that all of the other levels of Majesty build off of Awe and therefore contain the same risk is great for me. As Rose said, if you don't like that there's no reason you can't allow people to specify who they're not using it on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T21:12:27-08:00","id":37671,"title":"","content":"Indeed, I'd imagine the calculated risk as integral part of the Kindred's socio-political dance.<br /> <br /> Say you walk into a nightclub, and want to start turning on your supernatural charm and entice some lonely young thing to come home with you. So, you rev up your Awe, and the vampire who routinely hunts there Lashes Out against you for trying to steal her hunting ground. You have a few minutes before that vampire finds you in the crowd and enforces her territorial right.<br /> <br /> What do you do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T05:27:56-08:00","id":37801,"title":"","content":"That also implies Majesty is directly noticeable, though, which I've always assumed it wasn't. Anyone Lashing Out is either doing it because they wanted to lash out at you, discipline or not, or because they know you well enough to suspect they're under your charms. &quot;Oh, I'm under Majesty, better Lash Out...&quot; would make Majesty in Kindred circles rather pointless, as it's probably seen as a hostile move by the one using Majesty then. Its saving grace has always been that nobody can be absolutely sure at what instances you're using it or not using it, at least if you're charismatic even without it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T05:59:44-08:00","id":37811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37660#post37660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only for that one guy who Lashed Out though, everyone else is still affected, or so I thought. And anyway, it's not like that guy can't Lash Out at you if you don't use Majesty, so if Bestial, Competitive, or Wanton was going to ruin your day, it'd do so regardless of your disciplines. And like I said, I like discipline use to always be a risk in my games, so the fact that all of the other levels of Majesty build off of Awe and therefore contain the same risk is great for me. As Rose said, if you don't like that there's no reason you can't allow people to specify who they're not using it on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone else is still affected, but if you're trying to social-magic some people, very little will ruin your night (or <i>nights</i>, since Lashing Out Conditions last for more than one night) more than suddenly becoming skittish and scared, greedy and gluttonous for the sake of being greedy and gluttonous, or being given the choice of running through your willpower and becoming an abject failure. Essentially the inability to have single target or even limited target Majesty reverses the traditional positions of Majesty and its &quot;cousin&quot;, Dominate. Now Majesty is the hammer, with Dominate being the scalpel. Majesty being the Gross discipline, Dominate being the Subtle one.<br /> <br /> And yes, if you have an individual who is just going to Lash Out at people because he can, that is one thing and you (along with everyone else until the domain gets tired of their shit) are pretty much hosed no matter what you do. But you are significantly less likely to run into that type of Kindred than you are to run across a Kindred who is better off being excluded so as to not actively provoke them to action. (You can generally assume that anyone with &quot;Prince&quot; in their name falls into the second category)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37671#post37671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, I'd imagine the calculated risk as integral part of the Kindred's socio-political dance.<br /> <br /> Say you walk into a nightclub, and want to start turning on your supernatural charm and entice some lonely young thing to come home with you. So, you rev up your Awe, and the vampire who routinely hunts there Lashes Out against you for trying to steal her hunting ground. You have a few minutes before that vampire finds you in the crowd and enforces her territorial right.<br /> <br /> What do you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>You cry a little bit because however much you may want to be subtle, discrete, keep the First Tradition, focus on your prey of the evening and *not* become the most popular and idolized thing in this room full of mortal witnesses, the only thing you can do is make *everyone* in the room think you are the best thing ever and want to buy you all the drinks.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Ventrue across the street is picking and choosing a conga line of potential candidates like a razor-toothed wine critic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37801#post37801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That also implies Majesty is directly noticeable, though, which I've always assumed it wasn't. Anyone Lashing Out is either doing it because they wanted to lash out at you, discipline or not, or because they know you well enough to suspect they're under your charms. &quot;Oh, I'm under Majesty, better Lash Out...&quot; would make Majesty in Kindred circles rather pointless, as it's probably seen as a hostile move by the one using Majesty then. Its saving grace has always been that nobody can be absolutely sure at what instances you're using it or not using it, at least if you're charismatic even without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is not directly noticeable, then there is no reason for the Kindred in question to want to lash out to begin with. However, if someone walks in and once they get over to their chosen clique of harpies becomes &quot;cooler than you&quot; (as per Awe) without even saying as much as a word to you, then yeah, I would say that gets some attention. Another reason for the Daeva to cry a little because their 'scalpel' is Area-of-Effect and for the Ventrue to be smug bastards.<br /> <br /> As always, the rule of these things is of course &quot;if you don't like the rules, change them&quot;, I just want to make sure that this is the intended effect and if so, what the logic is before I get to the point where I'm considering house rules before the PoD book is even released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":323,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","user":"Hyoseph","date":". 12-27-2013, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T06:19:34-08:00","id":37823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it is not directly noticeable, then there is no reason for the Kindred in question to want to lash out to begin with. However, if someone walks in and once they get over to their chosen clique of harpies becomes &quot;cooler than you&quot; (as per Awe) without even saying as much as a word to you, then yeah, I would say that gets some attention. Another reason for the Daeva to cry a little because their 'scalpel' is Area-of-Effect and for the Ventrue to be smug bastards.<br /> <br /> As always, the rule of these things is of course &quot;if you don't like the rules, change them&quot;, I just want to make sure that this is the intended effect and if so, what the logic is before I get to the point where I'm considering house rules before the PoD book is even released. </div> </div> </div>The point is that when you lash out, you also end Majesty. That doesn't automatically bring with it that Majesty is immediately obvious. If he's cooler than you under the effects of Majesty, then it'll feel right and make sense for him to be, too. That's part of it. Nothing Majesty does at the lower levels is impossible. It makes someone incredibly alluring, but it's possible for someone to be. It makes your words seem very sensable and poignant, but it's possible that they are. Any Vampire who suspects they are under Majesty may lash out, but it's just that: a suspicion. They might be wrong, and if they are, they've just lashed out with no reason whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Anyone who wants to last in the Danse better make sure that they realize possible consequences for lashing out at anyone they suspect of Discipline use may very well be dire. Any game I'm Storyteller has the player guessing if that Kindred I'm describing as a magnet of personality is using Majesty... or just a strong, alluring personality. They'd do well to make sure which it is before taking rash actions, and they know this.<br /> <br /> I can't claim 100% that this is the intended writing, but nothing I've said is contradicted by the rules, it makes sense from a lore perspective (as the Daeva really have never been described as being super-obvious and easy to throw out of Elysium whenever they use a little Awe) and it's a lot more interesting from a gameplay perspective too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 12-27-2013, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T06:55:42-08:00","id":37832,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, Awe just makes all of your actions cast in the best possible light. So even if you become skittish or bloodthirsty or whatever from losing the Predatory Aura contest, it has no impact on how everyone who WAS affected will perceive you. They'll find you charming and likable no matter what you do. Also, I would say Lashing Out when affected by Majesty is a player choice (or ST choice for NPCS), not a character choice. The character doesn't notice that they are being affected by the discipline because that's just how Majesty works. It affects the minds of everyone who sees you, and they just think it's totally natural to be so into you, cause you're just that awesome. The Beast, on the other hand, doesn't always appreciate being manipulated, and will sometimes fight back of its own accord. It doesn't mean the person is consciously aware, just that their inner monster is rejecting the mind-affecting power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T07:28:16-08:00","id":37845,"title":"","content":"Oh, and judging by Rose's response, it sounds like the intention was probably for you to be able to exclude certain people from those AOE disciplines, so I think I'm the one house ruling otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T08:04:14-08:00","id":37866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37484#post37484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally, I think its realistic hazard of using mind-affecting powers that target large groups of people. You shouldn't be able to just turn on your love beams in a crowded room and expect no one to push back. And I don't think its reasonable to say &quot;well I'm only trying to impress the people who won't mind it&quot;. But that's just my personal taste, I like discipline use to always be a calculated risk. If that's not your bag, by all means allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my original intent with the power, and the way I ran it in playtest,* but I don't see a problem with &quot;targeted Awe.&quot;<br /> <br /> But it also seems like a reasonable thing to change (as you say, personal taste), and I can sort of see a Prince going &quot;well, I only want this one to play for the plebes&quot; and the Blood backing that up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37660#post37660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only for that one guy who Lashed Out though, everyone else is still affected, or so I thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct. Awe isn't an enchantment that just shatters if one person resists. If you lose a PA contest, you might be publicly humiliated, but you still look great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37801#post37801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That also implies Majesty is directly noticeable, though, which I've always assumed it wasn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't, and I'll put that in the FAQ. However, people retain enough faculties to go &quot;Martin looks smooth as silk and cool as air. Martin's a schlub. Since I know he's a Daeva and they can fuck with my head, maybe I ought to get in his face and make him back off whatever he's doing to me.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Which did in fact feature a predatory aura contest after someone injudiciously charmed a whole room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T08:19:13-08:00","id":37868,"title":"","content":"Am I correct in thinking that the Predatory Aura contest to resist is typically less of a conscious choice on the character's part, and more of The Beast instinctively reacting to a perceived challenge? Or was the intention that the subject has to intentionally decide they're going to Lash Out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T08:28:52-08:00","id":37875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37868#post37868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I correct in thinking that the Predatory Aura contest to resist is typically less of a conscious choice on the character's part, and more of The Beast instinctively reacting to a perceived challenge? Or was the intention that the subject has to intentionally decide they're going to Lash Out?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be either. A vampire often Lashes Out from instinct, but can also, feeling the aura of another vampire, consciously try to push back against that aura. Just like, when angry, you might punch a wall out of sheer frustration, but you can also choose to do so as a conscious expression of anger.<br /> <br /> (Or, I guess, hatred for walls.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T09:20:00-08:00","id":37894,"title":"","content":"I think it's important that we consider what would occur if we used the Predatory Aura on the object spirit of a Wall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T09:33:55-08:00","id":37899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37894#post37894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's important that we consider what would occur if we used the Predatory Aura on the object spirit of a Wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a Wall Spirit, I would expect it to be pretty chill and not give a fuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T10:55:18-08:00","id":37926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37866#post37866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't, and I'll put that in the FAQ. However, people retain enough faculties to go &quot;Martin looks smooth as silk and cool as air. Martin's a schlub. Since I know he's a Daeva and they can fuck with my head, maybe I ought to get in his face and make him back off whatever he's doing to me.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Which did in fact feature a predatory aura contest after someone injudiciously charmed a whole room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, of course you can assume a certain Daeva has Majesty on if all the signs point to it, I completely agree with that. As I said, that small bit of doubt about whether someone is using it makes the entire interaction just sooo much better, which I love. It's great design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T16:02:46-08:00","id":38049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=37899#post37899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being a Wall Spirit, I would expect it to be pretty chill and not give a fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>It experiences Wanton. It wants to keep being a wall so bad. It continues to be a wall. It is sated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T18:25:05-08:00","id":38099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=38049#post38049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It experiences Wanton. It wants to keep being a wall so bad. It continues to be a wall. It is sated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah that's not enough! It's been a wall every day of it's life until that sexy vampire punched it. It's been a very naughty wall and wants to be punished more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I honestly never thought I'd use a sentence like that... So we were talking about resisting disciplines...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1571-kamikazegerbil","name":"Kamikazegerbil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1571_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T14:27:41-08:00","id":1370849,"title":"","content":"I apologize for the necro, but I just re-read this entire post and my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1278551-lashing-out-against-some-powers\">own post</a> about the subject and my question is still unclear.<br /> <br /> The question is:<br /> <br /> Is it possible to Lash Out against someone that used Nightmare 1 on you if that person is using Obfuscate 3?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T15:02:27-08:00","id":1370861,"title":"","content":"Yes. When they used Dread Presence on you, they rendered you immune to all their uses of Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T16:56:05-08:00","id":1370880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=1370849#post1370849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to Lash Out against someone that used Nightmare 1 on you if that person is using Obfuscate 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, but that's not a fun approach so I'd allow it anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=1370861#post1370861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When they used Dread Presence on you, they rendered you immune to all their uses of Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. The victim <i>of an attack</i> automatically sees through Obfuscate. Dread Presence is far from being an attack. In fact, it's so subtle you might not even know who activated Dread Presence, especially if that person is invisible. You shouldn't even get the Wits+Composure roll for the person drawing attention to themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T21:37:58-08:00","id":1370935,"title":"","content":"Where does it state attacking someone with a discipline power doesn't count for purposes of eliminating Obfuscate or rendering victims immune to its application?<br /> How about an official errata to Dread Presence to retract the sentences where it says victims of Dread Presence know the source and vampires can Lash Out against the aura of fear created by Dread Presence with their predatory aura to avoid its effects was a misprint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T01:49:46-08:00","id":1370954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=1370935#post1370935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does it state attacking someone with a discipline power doesn't count for purposes of eliminating Obfuscate or rendering victims immune to its application?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=1370935#post1370935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about an official errata to Dread Presence to retract the sentences where it says victims of Dread Presence know the source</div> </div> </div> </div>Keyword you missed: &quot;subconsciously&quot;, implying that it's not consciously/knowingly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=1370935#post1370935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and vampires can Lash Out against the aura of fear created by Dread Presence with their predatory aura to avoid its effects was a misprint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, not what I said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:25:49-08:00","id":1371003,"title":"","content":"For me Dread Presence works quite the same as Awe (but with opposite effects). It makes your presence dreadful as Awe makes your presence astounding. You can't really be astounding without being seen. Same interpretation for Dread Presence imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:34:25-08:00","id":1371007,"title":"","content":"&quot;<b>Even if they barely notice her</b>, they feel a wave of fear and uncertainty.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;People feel like someone\u2019s watching them <b>even when they\u2019re otherwise alone</b>, [..]&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;People around her <b>subconsciously</b> register her as the cause of their fear, [..]&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Run it however you want (I don't mean that sarcastically; we also run it as being obvious) but don't bring in house rules without stating they're house rules in a rules discussion. How it works by RAW is that Dread Presence puts a blanket of unease over an area regardless of whether the victims realise it's your fault or not. If you're visible, they might realise it's you (especially if they interact with you; i.e. pay specific attention to you personally). If you're not visible, then they wouldn't even know someone else is there unless they deduct they're under the effects of Dread Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-28-2020, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:53:42-08:00","id":1371008,"title":"","content":"In other words they &quot;know&quot; something is there. Kind of like you &quot;know&quot; exactly where the refrigerator is located in your kitchen even though you can't see it from your bathroom<br /> <br /> House rules? You mean like you claiming that eroding someone's resistance, engendering an unnatural fear and revulsion in a specific person and depriving them of the ability to fight back doesn't constitute an attack?<br /> How about your house rule requiring visual line of sight on someone to Lash Out with their Predatory aura when the book says you only need to perceive the other's presence or in the specific case of Dread Presence, sense the aura in question.<br /> Maybe you're referring to your house rule that says Obfuscate continues to work as normal even on those who've been attacked or involuntarily obfuscated even though the book says otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T10:09:33-08:00","id":1371039,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn that Dread Presence affected the environment first, and then as an instant action the vampire could designate themselves as the source of the discomfort. Am I crazy?<br /> <br /> Edit: I can't find the reference at all -- not in Blood and Smoke, or the renamed version, or in the playtest doc. So I probably just mixed Dread Presence up with Face of the Beast. <br /> <br /> Ok, so, the description mentions that &quot;Even if they barely notice her, they feel a wave of fear and uncertainty. The world seems colder... People feel like someone's watching them even when they're otherwise alone,&quot; which tells me: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Victims don't automatically attribute the fear to anyone. There isn't necessarily any &quot;<i>That </i>guy is why I am afraid.&quot;</li> <li>That victims don't need to even be aware of the vampire's presence in order to be affected. A Nos could be hiding in the closet, and victims would be freaked out. That's at least coheres with the use of Obfuscate. And the wording is evocative of Obfuscate.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> That said, Obfuscate explicitly works by using/masking the predatory aura to make people not notice the vampire. <br /> <br /> I'd rule Dread Presence as able to be used with Obfuscate, but vampire victims will know there's another vampire nearby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 02-28-2020, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T10:41:46-08:00","id":1371046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=1371007#post1371007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<b>Even if they barely notice her</b>, they feel a wave of fear and uncertainty.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;People feel like someone\u2019s watching them <b>even when they\u2019re otherwise alone</b>, [..]&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;People around her <b>subconsciously</b> register her as the cause of their fear, [..]&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Run it however you want (I don't mean that sarcastically; we also run it as being obvious) but don't bring in house rules without stating they're house rules in a rules discussion. How it works by RAW is that Dread Presence puts a blanket of unease over an area regardless of whether the victims realise it's your fault or not. If you're visible, they might realise it's you (especially if they interact with you; i.e. pay specific attention to you personally). If you're not visible, then they wouldn't even know someone else is there unless they deduct they're under the effects of Dread Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the expressions: &quot;... For me&quot; and &quot;imho (in my opinion)&quot; is not clear for you? This is my way to read the discipline. Never wanted to state they are hard rules though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T12:35:04-08:00","id":1371068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36040-b-s-lashing-out-against-disciplines?p=1371046#post1371046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the expressions: &amp;quot;... For me&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;imho (in my opinion)&amp;quot; is not clear for you? This is my way to read the discipline. Never wanted to state they are hard rules though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologise for being so confrontative. I was steeling myself for whatever reply tsusasi would come up with.<br /> <br /> Despite that I was not prepared for the sheer amount of unashamed misrepresentation and passive aggression. I have no interest discussing any of this with you, tsusasi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}